## 9.2 CSR conversion

| Test File | Vertices | Edges | Input Type | Source | Expected Output | Actual Output | Time | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| graph_unweighted_10.txt | 10 | 29 | Unweighted adjacency list | 0 | CSR built, 58 stored entries | matches | 0.00122 ms | Pass |
| graph_unweighted_100.txt | 100 | 299 | Unweighted adjacency list | 0 | CSR built, 598 stored entries | matches | 0.011 ms | Pass |
| graph_unweighted_10000.txt | 10,000 | 29,999 | Unweighted adjacency list | 0 | CSR built, 59,998 stored entries | matches | 0.462 ms | Pass |
| graph_unweighted_50000.txt | 50,000 | 149,999 | Unweighted adjacency list | 0 | CSR built, 299,998 stored entries | matches | 1.945 ms | Pass |
| graph_unweighted_100000.txt | 100,000 | 299,999 | Unweighted adjacency list | 0 | CSR built, 599,998 stored entries | matches | 3.671 ms | Pass |
| graph_weighted_10.txt | 10 | 29 | Positive-weighted adjacency list | 0 | CSR built, 58 stored entries | matches | 0.002 ms | Pass |
| graph_weighted_100.txt | 100 | 299 | Positive-weighted adjacency list | 0 | CSR built, 598 stored entries | matches | 0.005 ms | Pass |
| graph_weighted_10000.txt | 10,000 | 29,999 | Positive-weighted adjacency list | 0 | CSR built, 59,998 stored entries | matches | 0.363 ms | Pass |
| graph_weighted_50000.txt | 50,000 | 149,999 | Positive-weighted adjacency list | 0 | CSR built, 299,998 stored entries | matches | 1.785 ms | Pass |
| graph_weighted_100000.txt | 100,000 | 299,999 | Positive-weighted adjacency list | 0 | CSR built, 599,998 stored entries | matches | 3.636 ms | Pass |

CSR entries stored = 2E for the undirected graphs above (each undirected
edge appears once in each endpoint's adjacency list, per section 6.1/7.1 of
the spec), which is why "CSR entries stored" is roughly double the edge
count E reported at the top of the file.

Generated graphs: random spanning path over vertices 0..V-1 (guarantees
every vertex is reachable from source 0) plus extra random edges for an
average degree of ~4, undirected, no self-loops or duplicate edges. Weighted
versions assign each edge a random integer weight in [1, 20].
